  <running_head>De Lingua Hebraica.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>literæ</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">rùm cùm Adamus nomina rebus impo-</l>
    <l n="2">neret,pauca illum nova(si tamen ulla:)</l>
    <l n="3">simplicia verba procudisse,sed vel com-</l>
    <l n="4">munia levi inflexione propria fecisse,</l>
    <l n="5">vel plura jungendo composuisse, res</l>
    <l n="6">ipsa loquitur : quanquam hodie mul-</l>
    <l n="7">torum rationem ignorari, tam multis</l>
    <l n="8">deperditis aut ignoratis radicibus, ne-</l>
    <l n="9">cesse est.</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">Proxima linguæ Hebraicæ dignitas,</l>
    <l n="11">Antiquitas, &amp; eorum, quibus illa ver-</l>
    <l n="12">nacula fuit, authoritas &amp; reverentia.</l>
    <l n="13">Nam si non sine ratione dixit emunctiss-</l>
    <l n="14">imæ naris &amp; judicii vir Quintilianus,</l>
    <l n="15">verba vetusta majestatem quandam</l>
    <l n="16">cum voluptate conjunctam afferre ora-</l>
    <l n="17">tioni : quanta sit illius linguæ majestas,</l>
    <l n="18">quæ alia non agnoscit incunabula, non</l>
    <l n="19">alios natales, quàm quos mundus ipse;</l>
    <l n="20">imò, si Rabbinis fides, non tam mundo</l>
    <l n="21">æqualis, quàm inter mundi causas nu-</l>
    <l n="22">meranda ? Ita enim illi vulgò loqui so-</l>
    <l n="23">lent, hanc esse linguam, in qua <i>creatum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>sit mundus</i>. Jam si manuscriptus codex</l>
    <l n="25">(ut annosas quercus &amp; exesos senio</l>
    <l n="26">lapides, multorum quondam populo-</l>
    <l n="27">rum numina, omittam:) si manuscri-</l>
    <l n="28">ptus, inquam, codex, cujus fugientes</l>
    <l n="29">literæ</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes />
</page>
